imes are distributed among the much sparser sequence $(S_n)_n$\nwith essentially the same density as in the positive integers, up to a factor of $2$.\n\n[MathOverflow 434111](https://mathoverflow.net/questions/434111/are-prime-numbers-among-sums-of-prime-numbers-distributed-as-frac-n2-lnn).\n\n[Me18] Meštrović, R., *Curious Conjectures on the Distribution of Primes\nAmong the Sums of the First `2n` Primes*, [arXiv:1804.04198](https://arxiv.org/abs/1804.04198)\n(2018)."}],"retention_basis":{"attribution":"MathOverflow question 434111 contributors","derivation":"Exact normalized Formal Conjectures declaration docstring from the bound Git revision.","license_spdx":"CC-BY-SA-4.0","retained_bytes":true,"retention_permission":"redistribution-permitted-under-license","source_locator":"https://mathoverflow.net/questions/434111/are-prime-numbers-among-sums-of-prime-numbers-distributed-as-frac-n2-lnn","source_rights_class":"MathOverflow material (CC-BY-SA-4.0)"}},"rights":{"formal_conjectures_record":{"attribution":"The Formal Conjectures Authors","license_spdx":"CC-BY-4.0","retention_permission":"redistribution-permitted-with-attribution"},"lean_source":{"attribution":"The Formal Conjectures Authors","license_spdx":"Apache-2.0","retention_permission":"redistribution-permitted-under-license"},"question_text":{"attribution":"MathOverflow question 434111 contributors","derivation":"Exact normalized Formal Conjectures declaration docstring from the bound Git revision.","license_spdx":"CC-BY-SA-4.0","retained_bytes":true,"retention_permission":"redistribution-permitted-under-license","source_locator":"https://mathoverflow.net/questions/434111/are-prime-numbers-among-sums-of-prime-numbers-distributed-as-frac-n2-lnn","source_rights_class":"MathOverflow material (CC-BY-SA-4.0)"},"third_party_source":{"attribution":"MathOverflow question 434111 contributors","caveat":"Only the attributed tracked docstring is retained as question text; no source-page or paper bytes are retained.","lic